  <tr>
    <td background="images/bg.gif"><font class=""><a href="modules.php?name=News&new_topic=31">Non Solo Madonna</a></font><br><font class="testo_notizia" color="#000000"><b>Deep Dish Announce George Is On Tour.</b></font></td>
  </tr>
  <tr height="1">
    <td  background="images/riga.gif"></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td bgcolor="#FFFFFF">
	<div align=justify><font class="storytext"><P>It’s been seven years since this Washington, DC duo released their fierce debut, Junk Science, a blistering mix of deep lush house, rock/dance fusion, jazz-tinged soul and moody atmospherics, and went on to become American leaders in the international dance arena, and to win a Grammy for their mix of Dido’s "Thank You" in 2002. <BR><BR>As well as being highly in-demand remixers (<STRONG>Madonna</STRONG>, Beth Orton, Depeche Mode, Dido, Janet Jackson, The Rolling Stones), Ali “Dubfire” Shirazinia and Sharam Tayebi have proven to be two of the most hard-working recording and touring artists in their own right and with their new album George Is On (due out July 12th) may well have delivered an collection that could prove to be the defining work of their careers. <BR><BR>Their <STRONG>George Is On world tour</STRONG> just kicked off in Australia, and they’re heading Stateside in July. <BR><BR>US Dates <BR><BR>7/1 Chicago, IL - Sound-bar <BR>7/2 Washington, DC - Fur <BR>7/3 Miami, FL - Space (*Dubfire Only) <BR>7/3 Los Angeles, CA - Avalon (*Sharam Only) <BR>7/8 Milwaukee, WI - The Rave <BR>7/12 Boston, MA - Axis <BR>7/13 Atlanta, GA - Eleven50 <BR>7/15 Los Angeles, CA - Avalon (*Dubfire Only) <BR>7/16 San Francisco, CA - Ruby Sky (*Dubfire Only) <BR>7/16 New York, NY - Crobar (*Sharam Only) <BR>7/20 Las Vegas, NV - ICE <BR>7/21 San Diego, CA - On Broadway (*Sharam Only) <BR>7/22 Seattle, WA - Medusa (*Sharam Only) <BR>7/23 Denver, CO - Red Rocks Festival </P>
<P>Source: <STRONG>Filter magazine</STRONG>.</P>
</font></div>
	</td>
  </tr>
  <tr height="1">
    <td background="images/riga.gif"></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
